   "outcomes": [
    "Demonstrate proficiency in the foundational skills and knowledge of occupational therapy as a profession, including anatomy, physiology, the history of the profession, and the principles of therapeutic use of self to effectively engage clients in meaningful activities.",
    "Apply ethical reasoning and the principles of therapeutic use of self to ensure client-centered and evidence-based practice.",
    "Integrate occupational therapy principles to design and implement interventions that address clients' unique needs, promoting engagement in meaningful and purposeful activities.",
    "Apply clinical reasoning and critical thinking skills to adapt interventions and utilize assistive technology, addressing the dynamic needs of clients across the lifespan.",
    "Advocate for the value of occupational therapy by collaborating with clients, families, and communities to enhance health, wellness, and quality of life through occupation-based approaches.",
    "Exhibit cultural humility and competence by respecting and integrating diverse cultural perspectives, values, and practices into therapeutic interactions and intervention planning.",
    "Maintain professionalism and develop a strong professional identity by upholding ethical responsibilities, demonstrating effective communication, engaging in life-long learning, and fostering inclusive environments within intra and inter- professional teams.",
    "Demonstrate competence in clinical skills, including observation, intervention planning, and documentation, to meet client goals and achieve successful outcomes in a variety of practice settings.",
    "Reflect on and integrate feedback from clinical experiences to continuously improve professional practice and client care delivery."
